Endpoint contract

URL called by the UI: ${LINE_API}/${company_id}?window=${timeframe}
timeframe is 7 or 30 (UI buttons).
Response must be HTTP 200 with this JSON shape (preferred and required):
[
{
"name": "<SYMBOL>",
"data": [
{ "x": "<ISO date or timestamp>", "y": <number>, "is_predicted": <bool> },
...
]
}
]
Fields:
x: ISO date string (e.g., "2026-03-20") or a timestamp useable by new Date().
y: number (close price).
is_predicted: true for forecasted points (these render dashed); false or omitted for actuals.
Sample that matches the “NABIL simulated” UI
[
{
"name": "NABIL",
"data": [
{ "x": "2026-03-20", "y": 450.5, "is_predicted": false },
{ "x": "2026-03-21", "y": 455.2, "is_predicted": false },
